    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761-a3">

                <pb facs="0886" n="790" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg790"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Goldschmidt to
                        Mr. Woodrick.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                                Guaira</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic">November 14,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Whereas yesterday, on the 13th day of November, 1899, there arrived in this port
                    the American steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Caracas</hi>, of Wilmington,
                    whereof you are master, <pb facs="0887" n="791" xml:id="pg791"/> late from New
                    York, and whereof you have failed to deposit at this consulate the register and
                    other ship’s papers of said steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Caracas</hi>, as
                    required by Revised Statutes of the United States, sections 4309 and 4310, as
                    per copies annexed, I, the undersigned, consul of the United States at this
                    port, therefore impose upon you a fine of $500, as per said law, as a penalty
                    for failure to deposit said papers in my care.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Goldschmidt</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
